= V1 public corpus inventory =

The V1 inventory is generated directly from the anonymous MediaWiki Action API rather than maintained manually page-by-page.

== Verified snapshot ==
Snapshot completed <code>2026-08-18T17:20:10Z</code>.

* 186 public pages across 24 nonnegative namespaces
* 606 archived public revision bodies
* 162 Main pages
* 9 actual Template pages
* 162 used category names / 0 created Category pages
* 4 authored Property pages
* 3 <code>smw/schema</code> pages
* 6 MediaWiki pages
* 2 File description pages / 2 file revision metadata records
* 0 retrievable historical file binaries / 2 explicitly recorded unavailable binary references
* 0 Concept pages
* 0 Module pages

The archive workflow reports <code>harvest: success</code>, <code>verify: success</code>, with no audit warnings.

== Canonical inventory surfaces ==
<pre>
archive-v1/audit.json                 completeness + exact counts
archive-v1-run-status.json            latest machine-run outcome
archive-v1/index.json                 every public page record
archive-v1/namespaces/*/index.json    exhaustive titles by namespace
archive-v1/pages/*                    exact current wikitext
archive-v1/history/*                  complete captured public revision bodies
archive-v1/templates/index.json       all 9 implemented templates
archive-v1/templates/usage/*          every template transclusion caller
archive-v1/categories/index.json      all 162 used/created category records
archive-v1/categories/members/*       complete category memberships
archive-v1/special/*                  exhaustive maintenance reports
archive-v1/files/index.json           file revision/binary availability evidence
</pre>

The generator follows MediaWiki continuation until no continuation token remains. It is implemented in <code>scripts/archive_v1.py</code> and run through the repository archive workflow.

== What exhaustive means here ==
The archive covers the public, anonymous-readable MediaWiki surface exposed through the Action API at snapshot time. It does not claim access to deleted/suppressed revisions, private data, or media whose historical binary bytes are no longer publicly resolvable.

For the two File records whose binary URLs now return 404, the metadata and resolution failure are preserved explicitly rather than treating those binaries as recovered.

== Interpretation ==
Archival capture establishes evidence. It does not automatically decide V2 disposition.

<pre>
archive exact source / revision / usage state
→ compare related versions
→ identify unique writing, semantics and behavior
→ distinguish design intent from deployed implementation
→ choose correct V2 primitive and disposition
→ publish / redirect / retire deliberately
</pre>

See [[BITwiki:V1 implementation audit]], [[BITwiki:V1 category migration]], [[BITwiki:V1 maintenance baseline]], [[BITwiki:Templates and categories]] and [[BITwiki:Editorial protocol]].

